  "finalText": "The loop is built: a 6 s, 1920×1080, 30 fps comp with five blurred orbs and a 12×7 dot grid, all driven by expressions. I checked frame 0 against frame 6 in a contact sheet and they match.\n\n- **Orbs:** five soft ellipses in purple, violet, teal and deep purple (blur 140–160 px, opacity 32–60%) drift in slow Lissajous paths.\n- **Dots:** 84 small white dots in four vertical bands. Each band's opacity pulses between roughly 10% and 38%, offset in phase left to right so a gentle wave crosses the grid.\n- **Seamless loop:** every motion is a sine or cosine with a whole number of cycles in 6 s (one or two per loop), so frame 6 equals frame 0 by construction with no keyframes to seam.\n- **Background:** deep navy `#0b0a1f`.\n\nThe critique scores it 80/100. Its one remaining flag is that the deep-purple orb bleeds off the bottom-right edge. I left that on purpose, since the orbs are blurred and a soft edge bleed suits an ambient stage background. If you want it fully inside the frame, I can pull it up.\n\nI didn't export a video. Say if you want an MP4 or a preview, or if you'd like the motion faster, the orbs larger, or the dots more visible."
